            <ArticleTitle>[Is medical/surgical false acute abdomen a clinical reality?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The false acute abdomen is a real Clinic picture. In pur experience it represents the 0.63% of acute surgical abdomen. Sometimes diagnosis could escage because patient's erethism. To obviate this event surgeons must reach a detailed history, perform a complete pshysical examination and repeat clinical evaluation many times above all when then the clinical picture is dubious. Laboratory and instrumental tests could be useful to reach accurate diagnosis. However, in our opinion, when clinical and physical examination are unclear, sometimes in spite of disappointment of other physicians, do explorative laparotomy is better is than non-treatment of an acute surgical abdomen. False acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
